World model: N6 remains at cols 15‑17 (blocked left). N7 is now at cols 39‑41 (moved left from 39‑41? actually unchanged, meaning the RIGHT‑LEFT pairs had no net effect on N7). It appears that moving RIGHT first shifts N6 right (and N7 right), then LEFT moves both left back to original positions, resulting in no net movement for either block. Thus the pair cannot be shifted left while N6 stays stuck. The N blocks move as a rigid unit; when N6 is against the left boundary of its magenta target, further LEFT moves have no effect on it, and consequently also do not move N7. Therefore the puzzle likely requires a different mechanic: perhaps clicking (MOUSE) on a magenta target when an N is touching it triggers completion. Since previous clicks had no effect, maybe the required action is to press a directional key that moves the combined N shape into the large magenta area at the bottom (c 12). That area spans rows 26‑30 and columns ... we need to locate it. Let's inspect magenta (c) objects.
